 "captions": [
  {
   "from_frame": 0,
   "duration_frames": 240,
   "text": "This is our whole bill for ten days. Seventeen dollars, seventy-eight cents. The number that matters is not on it."
  },
  {
   "from_frame": 240,
   "duration_frames": 300,
   "text": "Every tool you approve is priced by the month or by the seat. Your work does not happen by the month. It happens in runs."
  },
  {
   "from_frame": 540,
   "duration_frames": 288,
   "text": "So divide the bill by the number of times the task actually ran. Ours ran eight hundred and eighty-nine times. Two cents a run."
  },
  {
   "from_frame": 828,
   "duration_frames": 372,
   "text": "Here is the line that repeats every week. Last week, a hundred and thirty accounts, one page each. Two dollars sixty. That is the number to defend, not the plan name."
  },
  {
   "from_frame": 1200,
   "duration_frames": 324,
   "text": "What the bill leaves out: our own machine time, and sixteen cents we paid twice because a run broke halfway and eight answers had left the cache."
  },
  {
   "from_frame": 1524,
   "duration_frames": 276,
   "text": "Two cents a run is nothing. Two cents a run, six hundred times a day, is another conversation. Price the run, then decide."
  },
  {
   "from_frame": 1800,
   "duration_frames": 240,
   "text": "Before the next renewal, count how many times that task ran last month, then divide. Send this to whoever signs."
  }
 ],
